# Lark test ledger workflow

- Before generating or executing tests, read the project's requirement baseline.
- The canonical test ledger is `${LARK_BASE_URL}` and its configuration file is
  `.lark-test-ledger/ledger.env`. Do not silently create or switch to another Base.
- Generated full cases and submission cases use the same table. A non-empty
  `提测顺序` marks a submission case and defines its execution order.
- Generate `lark-test-ledger/v1` manifests, validate them, dry-run synchronization,
  and require explicit approval before committing generated definitions.
- Locate records by globally unique `用例ID`. Execution may update only `Date`,
  `Attachment`, `测试结果`, and `实际结果/备注`; preserve generated definitions.
- For browser-visible failures, capture evidence that shows the error or incorrect
  state. Append it to the same record. Preserve existing attachments. If evidence
  cannot be captured, record the reason in `实际结果/备注`.
- After every result or attachment write, reread the record and verify the change.

## Commands

Use `.lark-test-ledger/lark-ledger.ps1` from the project root:

```powershell
./.lark-test-ledger/lark-ledger.ps1 status
./.lark-test-ledger/lark-ledger.ps1 case list --submission-only
./.lark-test-ledger/lark-ledger.ps1 execution next
./.lark-test-ledger/lark-ledger.ps1 execution record --case-id TC-001 --result passed --notes "符合预期"
./.lark-test-ledger/lark-ledger.ps1 execution record --case-id TC-002 --result failed --notes "保存时报错" --evidence ./evidence/TC-002.png
```
